    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Genealogy of Jesus Christ"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "An account of the genealogy of Jesus Christ, the Son of David, the Son of Abraham:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "From Abraham to David"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Abraham fathered Isaac,",
          "Isaac fathered Jacob,",
          "Jacob fathered Judah and his brothers,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Judah fathered Perez and Zerah by Tamar,",
          "Perez fathered Hezron,",
          "Hezron fathered Aram,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Aram fathered Amminadab,",
          "Amminadab fathered Nahshon,",
          "Nahshon fathered Salmon,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Salmon fathered Boaz by Rahab,",
          "Boaz fathered Obed by Ruth,",
          "Obed fathered Jesse,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "and Jesse fathered King David."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "From David to the Babylonian Exile"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "David fathered Solomon by Uriah’s wife,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Solomon fathered Rehoboam,",
          "Rehoboam fathered Abijah,",
          "Abijah fathered Asa,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Asa fathered Jehoshaphat,",
          "Jehoshaphat fathered Joram,",
          "Joram fathered Uzziah,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Uzziah fathered Jotham,",
          "Jotham fathered Ahaz,",
          "Ahaz fathered Hezekiah,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Hezekiah fathered Manasseh,",
          "Manasseh fathered Amon,",
          "Amon fathered Josiah,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "and Josiah fathered Jeconiah and his brothers",
          "at the time of the exile to Babylon."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "From the Exile to the Messiah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "After the exile to Babylon",
          "Jeconiah fathered Shealtiel,",
          "Shealtiel fathered Zerubbabel,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Zerubbabel fathered Abiud,",
          "Abiud fathered Eliakim,",
          "Eliakim fathered Azor,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Azor fathered Zadok,",
          "Zadok fathered Achim,",
          "Achim fathered Eliud,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Eliud fathered Eleazar,",
          "Eleazar fathered Matthan,",
          "Matthan fathered Jacob,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "and Jacob fathered Joseph the husband of Mary,",
          "who gave birth to Jesus who is called the Messiah."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So all the generations from Abraham to David were fourteen generations; and from David until the exile to Babylon, fourteen generations; and from the exile to Babylon until the Messiah, fourteen generations."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Nativity of the Messiah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The birth of Jesus Christ came about this way: After his mother Mary had been engaged to Joseph, it was discovered before they came together that she was pregnant from the Holy Spirit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So her husband, Joseph, being a righteous man, and not wanting to disgrace her publicly, decided to divorce her secretly."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But after he had considered these things, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream, saying, “Joseph, son of David, don’t be afraid to take Mary as your wife, because what has been conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "She will give birth to a son, and you are to name him Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Now all this took place to fulfill what was spoken by the Lord through the prophet:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "See, the virgin will become pregnant",
          "and give birth to a son,",
          "and they will name him Immanuel,",
          "which is translated “God is with us.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When Joseph woke up, he did as the Lord’s angel had commanded him. He married her"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "but did not have sexual relations with her until she gave birth to a son. And he named him Jesus."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
